  "change": "Owned inflated buffer for plain eight-bit samples. Unfilter against already compacted previous rows and move each row left over filter bytes. All other native formats and Adam7 retain existing reconstruction. Buffered DEFLATE grows on demand, capping geometric allocation requests at the existing logical output limit; no allocation from declared PNG size is added.",
  "capacity_scope": "Returned byte-sample length remains exact. Inflation requests do not exceed the limit, so the normal global allocator retains at most the filtered size for the reused byte buffer; the existing zero row remains. No peak-memory measurement follows from these structural invariants."
}
